   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s041-u017",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "வசந்தன்",
    "text": "Hey, physician... medicine, medicine—you keep taking my life!",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-041.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-041.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s041-d013",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 66,
       "printed_page": 65
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "semantic-poetic",
     "notes": [
      "The literal `உயிரை வாங்குறே` sets up the physician's death-joke in the next exchange and is retained."
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s041-u018",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "வைத்",
    "text": "That's exactly what I'm trying to do, but it isn't happening!",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-041.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-041.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s041-d014",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 66,
       "printed_page": 65
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "semantic-poetic",
     "notes": [
      "The physician's reply preserves the dark comic reversal of `உயிரை வாங்க`."
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s041-u019",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "வச",
    "text": "What for? To take my life?",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-041.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-041.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s041-d015",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 66,
       "printed_page": 65
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "semantic-poetic"
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s041-u020",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "வைத்",
    "text": "Tch...tch... by God's grace, may your lifespan go on... this disease go on... and this humble servant's job go on; I am forever praying to Yama-Dharma for it.",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-041.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-041.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s041-d016",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 66,
       "printed_page": 65
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "semantic-poetic",
     "notes": [
      "The threefold `நீடிச்சு` repetition and the joke of praying to Yama-Dharma are preserved."
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s041-u021",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "வச",
    "text": "Physician! What is Yama's vehicle?",
